 "rules": [
  "Twenty-three measured regions on fourteen of the twenty-five pages account for every exhibit and every box the layout pass emitted: nine figure items, ten table rows and four refusals [caption.numbering].",
  "Nineteen exhibit designators print - Figures 1 to 9 and Tables 1 to 10, each exactly once - and every one of them owns a measured region, so the deficit is zero [caption.numbering].",
  "Only five of the nineteen designators are ever named in prose: Figure 2 on p7, a page before the art; Figure 4 on p9; Figure 5 on p10, a page AFTER the art; and Figures 6 and 7 on p19, the page they print on. The Figure 2 pointer breaks across baselines - \"as shown in Figure\" then \"2.\" - so a line-wise scan loses it, and the item records that line as its lead [mention.count].",
  "Two captions share one printed baseline on p8 (\"Figure 2: BP neural network structure  Figure 3: Training result\") and again on p9, and the captions pair with the panels by x, not by reading order: on p8 the raster network sketch at x85.8 is Figure 2 and the vector scatter at x310.7 is Figure 3 [caption.position].",
  "The p19 pair wraps in parallel columns, so the text layer interleaves the two captions line by line and neither is a substring of any printed line. Both are recorded as typed-from-crop, and the full printed text is \"Figure 6: The Jindong forest carbon storage in the next 100 years under the simulated harvesting situation\" and \"Figure 7: The carbon storage of Jindong forest wood products in the next 100 years under simulated harvesting conditions\" [caption.verbatim].",
  "Tables 3 and 5 print their colons with no following space (\"Table 3:Stepwise regression model coefficients\", \"Table 5:The variable coding and assignment of the model\"), so a caption detector that requires a space after the colon sees no caption on either page even though both print one [caption.numbering].",
  "Table 1 prints its caption on its own baseline at y 425.6 with the header cells at y 442.4, but the cached text layer merges the two into \"Symbol                                 Table 1: Notations\", which reads as a prose pointer to a table that nothing in the paper cites; the mention is recorded as zero on the word layer [mention.count].",
  "Every grid is a shaded Word table: three horizontal rules (top, under the header, bottom), not one vertical rule in the file, a darker header fill and alternating tints down the body. The rules themselves are 0.1 pt black filled rectangles sitting on 1.1 pt strokes, so a stroke-only counter sees two of the three [table.rule_style].",
  "Table 7 has no header row: the row under the top rule is already data, \"A(t)<20 ha -> Clear cutting, strip clear cutting\", and the left column merges the three slope groups 0-15, 15-25 and 26-35 degrees. header_rows must be at least 1, so the row is recorded header_rows 1 rows 7 with merged_cells true - the six body rows plus the first data row counted as the header [table.header_rows].",
  "Tables 6 and 10 both run over a page break without repeating their captions or their headers, so the continuation regions (p12 r1 and p21 r1) are refused as split-across-pages and the recorded row counts are the rows on the captioned page only - 6 and 5 - with continued true [table.continued].",
  "The units row of Table 8 draws its \"/\" and its \"\\u2014\" as eight tiny glyph images (10x18 and 17x18 px) inside the table box, so a rule that every exhibit region holds one raster would be fooled by a table region holding eight [geometry.family]."
